<thead>
<tr><th>#</th><th>Row</th><th>Existing APIs</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>

<tr>
<td>0</td>
<td class="rowlabel">Foundation — auto-attachment, classification &amp; filing</td>
<td>
<b>Account/policy match:</b> <code>account</code>: <code>GET /accounts/search?email=</code> / <code>?phoneNumber=</code>; <code>client</code>: <code>GET /clients?email=&amp;phoneNumber=&amp;name_contains=&amp;address_contains=</code>; <code>policy</code>: <code>GET /clients/{clientId}/policies?policyNumber=</code>.<br>
<b>Filing:</b> <code>attachment</code>: <code>POST /attachments</code>, <code>POST /attachments/{attachmentId}/attach-to</code>.<br>
<b>Activity note:</b> <code>workflow-management</code>: <code>POST /activities</code> / <code>POST /system-activities</code>, <code>POST /activities/{activityId}/notes</code>.<br>
<span class="gap">Classification itself is not an Epic API</span> — happens upstream of these calls.
</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>1</td>
<td class="rowlabel">COI Agent — email-trigger detection (additive)</td>
<td>
<code>policy</code>: <code>GET /policies/{policyId}</code>, <code>GET /clients/{clientId}/policies</code>, <code>GET /lines/{lineId}</code> (coverage verification).<br>
<b>Filing the issued cert:</b> <code>attachment</code>: <code>POST /attachments</code> (type <code>CERTIFICATE</code>).<br>
<b>Reply:</b> <code>configure</code>: <code>POST /email-templates/{templateId}/generate-email-content</code>.<br>
Cert issuance itself runs through CSR24, not an Epic API — consistent with the workstream's own note that COI MVP has no Epic API dependency.
</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>2</td>
<td class="rowlabel">Evidence of Insurance &amp; Auto ID Card (reuses COI pattern)</td>
<td>
Same shape as Row 1: <code>policy</code> for coverage lookup, <code>attachment</code> + <code>attachment-folder</code> for filing/retrieving the issued document, <code>configure</code> for the reply.<br>
<span class="gap">No VIN / vehicle-schedule endpoint exists anywhere in the catalog</span> — relevant specifically to Auto ID Card's vehicle-level identification.
</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>3</td>
<td class="rowlabel">Service inquiry resolution — coverage/billing/claims (leverages Max Search)</td>
<td>
<b>Coverage:</b> <code>policy</code>: <code>GET /policies/{policyId}</code>, <code>/lines/{lineId}/policy-information</code>.<br>
<b>Billing:</b> <code>accounting</code>: <code>GET /clients/{clientId}/transactions</code>, <code>GET /payment-transactions/{referenceId}</code>.<br>
<b>Claims status:</b> <code>policy</code>: <code>GET /clients/{clientId}/claims</code>.<br>
<b>Doc-pull:</b> <code>attachment</code>: <code>GET /attachments</code>.<br>
<i>Max Search itself isn't one of the 41 catalogued services</i> — whether it calls these endpoints directly or sits on a separate index isn't answerable from the catalog alone.
</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>4</td>
<td class="rowlabel">Endorsement / change request intake (next agent)</td>
<td>
<b>Validate current policy:</b> <code>policy</code>: <code>GET /policies/{policyId}</code>, <code>/lines/{lineId}</code>.<br>
<b>Create CHGE activity:</b> <code>workflow-management</code>: <code>POST /activities</code>.<br>
<span class="gap">The carrier-facing endorsement transaction itself is a confirmed gap</span> — no <code>endorsement</code> service/endpoint exists anywhere in the 41-service catalog, matching the workstream's own "API availability is still TBD."<br>
<span class="gap">Missing-data fields called out (VIN, payroll, AI details) are also confirmed gaps</span> — no vehicle/VIN endpoint, and no payroll endpoint anywhere (checked <code>benefits-configure</code>, the only benefits-adjacent service — it's plan configuration, not payroll/exposure data).
</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>5</td>
<td class="rowlabel">Activity-triggered outbound communications (closes the loop)</td>
<td>
<b>Draft:</b> <code>configure</code>: <code>POST /email-templates/{templateId}/generate-email-content</code>.<br>
<b>Log as filed:</b> <code>workflow-management</code>: <code>POST /activities/{activityId}/notes</code>.<br>
<span class="gap">The trigger mechanism itself is a confirmed gap</span> — no webhook/event-subscription endpoint anywhere in the catalog; the <code>activity</code> service's <code>GET /events</code> is reference data (event <i>type</i> definitions), not a live event feed.<br>
Send itself is Microsoft Graph, not an Epic API.
</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>6</td>
<td class="rowlabel">Internal collaboration &amp; administration (largest category, mostly second-order)</td>
<td>
Slices A &amp; B reuse Row 0's account-match + <code>workflow-management</code> activity-creation APIs exactly — no new APIs.<br>
Slice C (discussion/FYI) has no applicable API — organizational/behavioral, not an integration gap.
</td>
</tr>

</tbody>
