<div class="finding">
<h2>Finding worth flagging back to Chase / Anupam / John Rush</h2>
Row 0 states: "Account-match remains the hard part: 25% by business name, 22% policy number, 19% name — all unresolvable today." Checked against the API layer, <code>GET /clients/{clientId}/policies?policyNumber=</code> and <code>GET /clients?name_contains=</code> <b>do exist</b> for exactly the policy-number (22%) and name (19%) buckets. If those are still "unresolvable," the blocker is more likely match-confidence/disambiguation logic (multiple candidates, fuzzy name matching) than a missing endpoint — a meaningfully different problem to scope than "no API exists," and worth confirming before it shapes the Row 0 build plan.
</div>

